% Aggregates in queries written in the program.  A query's output columns
% are the rule's named variables, so a body's own variables take none.  Two
% queries with an aggregate at the same position share nothing but the
% generated predicate's entry, and each derives its own group.
edge(a, b). edge(a, c). edge(b, c). edge(c, a).
node(a). node(b). node(c). node(d).

node(X), N = count { edge(X, Y) }?
node(X), N = count { edge(Y, X) }?
N = count { edge(X, Y) }?
node(X), N = count { edge(X, Y) }, N > 1?
S = sum(D) { edge(X, Y), node(Y), D = 1 }?
